# Cloudflare Workers static-assets response headers (review findings P2-8/9,
# 2026-10-21). Cloudflare reads this file from the build output (Vite copies
# public/ → dist/client/). GitHub Pages ignores it (it is served as a plain
# file there and has no effect). Rationale + how to verify: docs/security-headers.md
#
# The /* block below MUST stay identical to SECURITY_HEADERS in
# src/lib/security-headers.ts (the single source of truth; CSP rationale is
# documented there). src/lib/security-headers.test.ts fails on drift.
#
# Scope: Cloudflare applies this file to STATIC ASSET responses only. It is
# NOT applied to Worker-generated responses, and the live `meridian` worker
# server-renders the HTML. Those responses get the same headers from the
# request middleware in src/start.ts.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://server.arcgisonline.com; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://server.arcgisonline.com https://meridian-crash-report.knowledgetest.workers.dev https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Carve-outs (Core F-1): NOT every file under /assets/* is content-hashed.
# Three files have stable names with mutable content and must never be
# immutable:
#   - /assets/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs and /assets/maplibre-gl-shared.mjs
#     are emitted verbatim from node_modules/maplibre-gl/dist by the
#     maplibre-worker-files plugin in vite.config.ts — a MapLibre
#     upgrade replaces them under the SAME filenames.
#   - /assets/storyteller/storyteller-assets.json is a build-generated
#     manifest fetched at runtime by storyteller-home.tsx — its content
#     changes whenever the storyteller asset set changes, same filename.
#
# How the rules combine — the semantics below are Cloudflare's documented
# behaviour (developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/),
# confirmed against the production asset-worker's source
# (cloudflare/workers-sdk, asset-worker/src/utils/headers.ts,
# attachCustomHeaders) and live probes of the deployed site:
#   - A request inherits the headers of EVERY rule whose pattern it
#     matches. Matched rules are applied in file order, and within one
#     rule all detachments run before all sets.
#   - The FIRST Cache-Control set from this file REPLACES whatever the
#     response already carries (including the platform default). A SECOND
#     set of the same header from this file APPENDS instead — the values
#     comma-join. There is no most-specific-wins, so ordering and
#     detachment are the only tools; that is what the blocks below use.
#   - A detach line (`! Cache-Control`) DELETES the response's current
#     Cache-Control at the point its rule is applied. PR #203 used
#     detach ALONE for the carved files, expecting the platform default
#     to resume underneath — it does not: the default is part of the
#     response being edited, so the detach removed it too, and the
#     carved files shipped with NO Cache-Control at all (live-verified
#     2026-10-21: ETag present, Cache-Control absent). Each carved block
#     therefore pairs the detach with an explicit set in the SAME block:
#     the wildcard's immutable value is deleted first, then the set
#     stands alone as the path's only Cache-Control value. One block per
#     path — the platform keys rules by their URL pattern, so a second
#     block for the same path would not be a separate rule.
#
# HTML, /flags.json and the sw.js group: every one gets an explicit
# line below, so this file — not an undocumented platform default —
# is the caching contract of record for them, with one exception:
# for rendered HTML the contract of record is the Worker middleware
# (see the honesty note below); this file's HTML lines only cover an
# asset-served copy. Each is the first and
# only Cache-Control set matching its path, so each simply replaces
# the platform default.
# One honesty note: the root document at / is currently rendered by the
# app server, not served as a static asset (live probe 2026-10-21: the
# / response carries neither the ETag nor the CF-Cache-Status header
# the asset server always adds), so the / rule below cannot reach it on
# the Cloudflare host today. It is kept so the policy lives in one place
# and takes effect for any asset-served root. The server-side header
# that note once called for now exists (WI-18, 2026-10-22): the request
# middleware in src/start.ts sends the rendered pages' Cache-Control
# itself, so a post-merge live probe of / should show the middleware's
# value (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate); the _headers rule remains
# for asset-served roots only. /offline.html is served
# as an asset at its canonical path /offline (the .html URL 307-redirects
# there), so it IS covered. /_shell.html is different: it exists in the
# build output, but a live probe (2026-10-21) shows GET /_shell.html
# answering 404 from the app server — the same signature as / — so the
# rule below cannot reach it today either. It is kept as policy of
# record, and a bare or 404 probe result for it is expected-inert, not
# a failure (see the Acceptance definition in BRANCH_STATUS.md).
#
# Unioned with main 2026-10-22 (#207/#222 landed first, adding the /*
# security block and the no-cache / s-maxage blocks below). Where the
# two files set the same path, MAIN'S VALUE WINS and appears exactly
# once: /flags.json is no-cache (stricter than the max-age=0 line this
# branch proposed — a kill switch must never be served stale) and / is
# main's s-maxage=60 edge line. What this branch contributes is the
# detach+set form on the three carved /assets/ paths and the
# /offline, /offline.html and /_shell.html rules.
#
# Deliberately NO rule: everything not listed below is already served
# with the platform default (Cache-Control: public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate, plus an ETag) — live-verified 2026-10-21 for
# /audio/*, /icons/*, /images/*, /loop/*, favicon.svg and og.jpg. Those
# paths have stable names with mutable content (narration mp3s were
# replaced under the same filenames in PR #174), so revalidation is
# exactly right for them, and adding set lines would only create
# comma-join surface if a broader rule ever lands above them. They must
# NEVER become immutable. (The other stable-named files — /sw.js,
# /flags.json, /build-meta.json, /manifest.webmanifest — DO carry
# explicit no-cache rules below; update detection and kill switches are
# too important to leave to a default.)

# Hashed build assets never change at a given URL → cache for a year.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ...except the three UN-hashed files that live under /assets/ (stable names,
# mutable content): the MapLibre worker copies (maplibre-worker-files plugin
# in vite.config.ts) and the storyteller asset manifest. Cloudflare joins
# headers from every matching rule (no most-specific-wins), so a second
# Cache-Control set-line would comma-join with "immutable". Each block
# therefore pairs a detach line with an explicit set in the SAME block:
# the detach deletes the wildcard's immutable value, then the set stands
# alone (see "How the rules combine" above — PR #203's detach ALONE shipped
# these files with no Cache-Control at all, live-verified 2026-10-21).
/assets/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/maplibre-gl-shared.mjs
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/storyteller/storyteller-assets.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The service worker and the files it treats as "latest" must revalidate
# every time, or update detection (fingerprinted sw.js) and remote kill
# switches (flags.json) stall.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/flags.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/build-meta.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# HTML entry points: these two rules only ever reach an ASSET-SERVED
# copy of the document. The live site's HTML is rendered by the Worker,
# which sends Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate from
# the request middleware in src/start.ts (constant HTML_CACHE_CONTROL
# in src/lib/security-headers.ts) — deliberately WITHOUT s-maxage,
# since rendered pages can carry per-request state. These rules are
# kept as the policy of record for any asset-served root.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60, must-revalidate

# Served as assets and not covered above. /offline.html is reachable at
# its canonical path /offline (the .html URL 307-redirects there);
# /_shell.html is in the build output but currently answers 404 from the
# app server, so its rule is policy of record and expected-inert today.
/offline
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/offline.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/_shell.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
